codex
A more substantive idea: because this ReLU MLP has no biases, it is positively homogeneous. For Gaussian input `X = R U`, the target mean equals `E[R] * E[f(U)]`. I’m going to sample only directions by normalizing each QMC input to a fixed radius `E[R]`, which should remove radial Monte Carlo variance while preserving the desired expectation.
